# P02A reproductions (docs/reviews/P02-review.md), 2026-10-04, M2 Pro, macOS 27.0 (26A5353q)

## Finding 1: installed commands fail with "No module named 'floscan'"

Before the fix (16:28 IST), plain shell, no PYTHONPATH:
$ ls -lO .venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/floscan.pth
-rw-r--r--@ 1 dakshtaneja  staff  hidden  38  4 Oct 16:15 .venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/floscan.pth
$ .venv/bin/python -c "import floscan"
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'floscan'          exit=1
$ uv run --locked floscan --help
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'floscan'          exit=1

Every entry of .venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages carried UF_HIDDEN, and so did
.venv itself, .git, .gitignore, .pytest_cache and .ruff_cache. Non-dot paths
(src/, configs/) did not. Flag change times (ctime) were 15:37-16:17, after the
files were created (13:55-16:15), so the flag is applied later by another agent.

Not uv: the uv cache (~/.cache/uv) had no hidden flags, and after clearing the
flag on floscan.pth a `uv run --no-sync floscan --help` (exit 0) left it clear.

Cause: this Desktop is synced by iCloud Drive.
$ defaults read com.apple.finder FXICloudDriveDesktop
1
$ ls -la ~/Library/Mobile\ Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs | grep Desktop
Desktop -> /Users/dakshtaneja/Desktop
Other Desktop projects show the same flag: helix-agent/.venv and yt2mp4/.venv are hidden.
CPython 3.11.15's site.addpackage skips .pth files that have UF_HIDDEN.

Probe (created 16:29:57; flags checked every 15 s until 16:40):
  .p02a_probe_dot/lib/probe.pth           hidden within 5 s (16:30:02), stayed hidden
  .p02a_probe_dot.nosync/lib/probe.pth    never hidden
  p02a_probe_plain/lib/probe.pth          never hidden
  p02a_probe.nosync/lib/probe.pth         never hidden
iCloud hides dot-named paths unless they are excluded with the .nosync suffix.

Fix: scripts/bootstrap.sh keeps the environment in .venv.nosync with .venv a
symlink to it (16:32). Watch of .venv.nosync, floscan.pth, torch/__init__.py and
the .venv link, every 15 s from 16:32 to 16:40: never hidden. A plain
`uv sync --locked` kept the symlink. Python's .pth safeguard is untouched.

## Finding 2: doctor report filesystem errors escape the CLI

Before the fix, output parent is a regular file (doctor report stubbed to isolate
the output boundary; scratch script, PYTHONPATH=src used for this diagnostic only
because finding 1 was still open):
$ floscan doctor --output blocker/report.json
  args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
FileExistsError: [Errno 17] File exists: '.../blocker'      exit=1 (traceback)
blocker preserved: "keep me"

After the fix:
floscan doctor: error: cannot prepare report path .../blocker/report.json: [Errno 17] File exists: '.../blocker'
exit=1, one line, no traceback, blocker preserved. The check runs before the
doctor's checks, so a bad path no longer costs minutes of model runs.
